#
# What the Cut Room's scripts import, as the workflow they come from lists it,
# with Pillow, which it used without listing. NumPy, Pillow, and Pedalboard are
# held at the versions that workflow's settings were settled on (the voice
# masters, the keying, and the headline's measured width); the others are the
# newest that resolve, yt-dlp above all, which the sites it reads outdate
# within weeks. `python.lock` is this file resolved to exact versions, every
# wheel with its hash, for the Python of the base image (3.14, on glibc 2.39
# or newer); the image installs the lock and nothing else (`install.sh
# python`). To move a pin, edit this file or leave it and run, in this folder:
#
#     uv pip compile python.in --python-version 3.14 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_39 \
#         --only-binary :all: --generate-hashes --no-header --no-annotate -o python.lock
#
# then build the image, whose last step loads every package and model.
